      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KARLAN: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The government violates the First Amendment whenever it retaliates against someone because they exercise -- criticize public policies or public officials. And this is so even when the retaliation takes the form of an arrest for which there's probable cause. Section 1983, by its terms, provides an action at law that is a damages action anytime someone is deprived of a right secured by the Constitution. And that statute should apply here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-21",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0ee1efe9d238c6a6856a6c1729ffaa35c02d2e38e4b1dbd55bc317fc7faffa06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee1efe9d238-0001-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court dismissed the case either on a 12(b)(6) motion or on a summary judgment on the grounds that there was not sufficient evidence to go to a jury on retaliatory animus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-21",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0ee1efe9d238c6a6856a6c1729ffaa35c02d2e38e4b1dbd55bc317fc7faffa06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee1efe9d238-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If that -- if that is so, then the First Amendment is in trouble."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2017-17-21",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0ee1efe9d238c6a6856a6c1729ffaa35c02d2e38e4b1dbd55bc317fc7faffa06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee1efe9d238-0001-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "evidence that there was a pre-determined plan to arrest somebody on account of his political speech in a political forum."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-21",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "0ee1efe9d238c6a6856a6c1729ffaa35c02d2e38e4b1dbd55bc317fc7faffa06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee1efe9d238-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: -- but -- but none -\u00ad none -- none -- nonetheless, what -- what harm would happen to the interests that you've heard articulated?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-21",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "0ee1efe9d238c6a6856a6c1729ffaa35c02d2e38e4b1dbd55bc317fc7faffa06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee1efe9d238-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "The harm that would happen is that this Court has repeatedly recognized that police officers need objective bright-line rules, not five- or six- or seven-factor tests that they then need to apply on the ground."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Alaska",
      "case_id": "2017-17-21",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "0ee1efe9d238c6a6856a6c1729ffaa35c02d2e38e4b1dbd55bc317fc7faffa06",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0ee1efe9d238-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sorry. As -- I did go through the list that the Alaska brief formed and the six that you -- that you listed. It seems to me that having read those cases, that they went to trial not because those limitations failed but because there was other evidence of things that -- that -- that didn't fail but made this triable cases."
    },
